<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mewar Praja Mandal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mewar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/praja-mandal">Praja Mandal</a> was a people's association founded in 1938 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manikya-lal-varma">Manikya Lal Varma</a> in the princely state of Mewar (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a>) to campaign for civil liberties, responsible government and relief from feudal dues. Banned by the state soon after its foundation, it was part of the praja mandal movement linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-national-congress">Indian National Congress</a>, and its leader became prime minister of the United State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> in 1948.</p></div>
